 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Keep it in the fridge or the freezer. A cool cooler with ice packs works perfectly. Blocks are much cheaper, and they melt slower than ice cubes. Just wrap them in a damp cloth or an old towel. Pack it as tight as you can, so it stays cold longer. A layer of wet towels on top of it keeps it from getting too cold. Then you' doing it right. Tight packing and a layer of towels keep it cold. Yes, and keep the containers out of the fridge. Melted water can make it sweat and smell.",
